<!--BYPROD-START-->
<section id="bp" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t-bp">
  <h2>By product</h2>
  <p class="sub">Each product and its release cycles. Click a cycle chip to open it in the release explorer.</p>
  <div class="toolbar"><input id="bpSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search products" aria-label="Search products"></div>
  <div id="bpGrid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:12px"></div>
</section>

<!--PIT-START-->
<section id="pit" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t-pit">
  <h2>Point in time</h2>
  <p class="sub">Choose a date to see the status of every release cycle on that day. Dates are calculated from the release, end-of-life and extended-support dates.</p>
  <div class="toolbar">
    <label for="pitDate" class="muted" style="align-self:center">Date</label>
    <input type="date" id="pitDate" min="1994-01-01" max="2035-12-31" value="2026-10-20" aria-describedby="pitNote">
    <button type="button" id="pitReset" style="font:inherit;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #c8cfda;background:#fff;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer">Reset to 20 Oct 2026</button>
    <select id="pitOS" aria-label="Filter by product"></select>
    <select id="pitStatus" aria-label="Filter by status"></select>
    <input id="pitSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search product or cycle" aria-label="Search">
  </div>
  <div class="pit-kpis" id="pitKpis"></div>
  <div class="count" id="pitCount"></div>
  <div class="tw pit-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Cycle</th><th>Codename</th><th>Released</th><th>End of life</th><th>Extended support ends</th><th>Status on selected date</th></tr></thead><tbody id="pitBody"></tbody></table></div>
  <div class="card" id="pitNote" style="margin-top:14px;font-size:14px">
    <b>How this is calculated</b>
    <ul class="notes" style="margin:6px 0 0 18px;padding:0">
      <li>Not yet released: the release date is after the selected date.</li>
      <li>Supported, Ending within 12 months (end of life within 365 days of the selected date), or Extended support, using the end-of-life and extended-support dates.</li>
      <li>Unsupported (EOL passed): the end-of-life date is on or before the selected date and no extended support date is still in the future.</li>
      <li>Cycles with no end-of-life date are shown as Supported (no EOL date) or Unsupported (no EOL date) using the current source status. The source does not record when these changed, so their status on past dates is an approximation.</li>
      <li>OpenBSD 7.8 has an end-of-life date of 20 Oct 2026. On that date it shows as Unsupported (EOL passed) here, but Supported in the All cycles and Overview tabs.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

